#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:5
#: 129095dfaa4a438e87a32c6f4b60f8be
msgid "LIDAR-Lite Rangefinder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:7
#: 709a4f1b84a04fa68047e1f4aafabbf6
msgid "The `Garmin / PulsedLight LIDAR-Lite <https://support.garmin.com/support/manuals/manuals.htm?partNo=010-01722-00>`__ rangefinder is a low-cost optical distance measurement solution with a 40m range under most operating conditions, low power consumption, and small form factor.  This sensor can be purchased from many online retailers including `Sparkfun <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/14032>`__.  Technical info can be found `here <https://support.garmin.com/support/manuals/manuals.htm?partNo=010-01722-00>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:13
#: b31041a1f72941c3a61c323579cdbc8e
msgid "Problems with the Lidar-Lite v1 & v2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:15
#: 24f2d9ed3beb4ed5a075609f903cf69d
msgid "A number of problems have been found with the Lidar-Lite v1 & v2 and it is not yet clear if these issues are resolved in v3. Attempts to resolve these issues with the manufacture have not been entirely successful. These notes serve as a warning to potential users."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:17
#: b78ac5c184fa43049dd39a19f35ed8ad
msgid "The problems are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:19
#: 48d6d9826ea24d60a835af684731a448
msgid "13m offset from true distance on both \"blue-label\" and \"black-label\" Lidars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:20
#: 9b1c831bcc1d49ec8297781f6fe12682
msgid "Interference with other I2C devices when using \"blue-label\" Lidars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:21
#: 085439130e3f40539e9302deaa217d87
msgid "Sensor lock-ups when using I2C with the older \"black-label\" Lidars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:22
#: f7e5a2a99d87436dbbc594e956cc26ab
msgid "GPS interference with the older \"black-label\" Lidars"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:25
#: 59dcd8f0898943bcb90981fbc2ee202f
msgid "13m offset (Blue-Label and Black-Label Lidars)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:27
#: e029f1c973b44d53a9abe81dfec9e26e
msgid "The lidar will sometimes (rarely) return a distance of approximately 13m greater than the true distance. This happens on both I2C and PWM. The problem has been recorded in several flight logs on several different aircraft and has also been reproduced in extensive bench testing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:29
#: 3c14ba18a8554ff08ff6c7b543ffd93b
msgid "When the problem happens the 13m offset usually locks in place, so all remaining readings from the Lidar for the rest of the flight will give a 13m offset. There have however been cases where the 13m offset disappears after a few seconds or minutes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:31
#: eeb6802d2325487c9c1fc6ea7a2c36f9
msgid "The problem is much more likely to occur if the Lidar power supply fluctuates too much. The problem can be easily reproduced in a bench setup where the Lidar is initially powered at below 4V then the voltage raised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:33
#: 3254b856537f4d1da0165430661d1098
msgid "Unfortunately low supply voltage is not the only trigger for the problem, so ensuring a good power supply will reduce the probability of the issue but not eliminate it. Multiple flight logs where the supply voltage to the Lidar is being monitored show the problem can occur with a good power supply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:35
#: 8b6e5224874544b4b14afc7c316db4e8
msgid "There is no known workaround for this issue. Detailed traces of the issue have been provided to the makers of the device with no resolution. The issue has also been reproduced using the device makers own software and own recommended hardware setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:38
#: 8ea2b022aa694dbb801b94847ac0ff1b
msgid "I2C interference (Blue-Label Lidars)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:40
#: 3da5f4a7794444a6a2573c4459ae5f2f
msgid "The newer blue-label Lidars have been associated with interference problems on I2C with other I2C devices on the same bus. In particular, incorrect airspeed readings have been seen when used on the same I2C bus as a digital airspeed sensor. This issue does not occur in all aircraft, but when it does occur the results are quite dramatic, with airspeed readings being off by more than 10m/s."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:42
#: 3bb019a3a66c4756946bef753be27e50
msgid "Although bench testing has reproduced the result we have not yet managed to capture a logic trace of it happening. The problem is solved by using the Lidar via PWM instead of I2C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:45
#: 4d7b66d8572647d18f5c012804d7070e
msgid "Sensor Lock-up on I2C (Black-Label Lidar)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:47
#: 005c52e079f240fdbbe87fc121127c69
msgid "The first issue (Lock-ups on I2C with black-label lidars) is solved by either using the new blue-label Lidars or by using the PWM output method, preferably with a reset pin. The issue is not common, but it is relatively easy to reproduce in bench tests by covering the Lidars lenses. It appears to be more likely to happen when the Lidar is reading short distances. There are two manifestations of the issue - one is where the lock-up is solved by sending a I2C reset command, the other does not respond to an I2C reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:50
#: 3474ea60ac174745b8f5502593afe3f3
msgid "GPS Interference (Black-Label Lidars)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:52
#: e36dbc03c361453bb18e97f1ddde108b
msgid "The older black-label Lidars cause significant GPS interference. This manifests as longer time to get GPS lock on power up and higher levels of GPS noise when lock is achieved resulting in lower GPS accuracy. Testing shows that the interference includes both a conducted and radiated component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:54
#: 466e265dfd39472c9dd8f3b20a4b328d
msgid "Placing the Lidar as far away from the GPS as possible helps, but does not entirely eliminate the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:57
#: 7dc7aa40853a41e58efb4fd7fddaf446
msgid "Connecting via I2C"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:61
#: 94f5dc017fd8470c81630ac2cce838c3
msgid "Lidar-Lites manufactured before Feb 2015 have I2C interface communications issues.  For these lidar please connect using PWM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:63
#: d5c62bae701c4c55a6bceebdbae25197
msgid "The connector cable has a 6-pin CLIK-Mate connector on one end and tinned leads on the other.  The leads should be soldered to a DF13 or JST connector and connected to the autopilot's I2C port as shown below"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:65
#: 1fb0bf3d8944418b8f00e2b41abb84b0
msgid "The power to the rangefinder should be supplied from a separate external BEC as shown in the diagram below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:71
#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:89
#: ../../source/docs/common-rangefinder-lidarlite.rst:110
#: 130d6b08f1da4367b4e3ce625d0aadc3
#: d0ca8759357c47c7bab11c5397a9deb5
